This part results in three files:
- class1_sequences.fasta: sequences of hits classified as Class I
- class2_sequences.fasta: sequences of hits classified as Class II
- proteomes_filtered.tsv: proteome metadata with viral proteomes removed
  (equivalent to proteomes_metadata.tsv)

And in two tables:
- table1_class1.csv: Class I distribution across taxonomic groups
- table2_class2.csv: Class II distribution across taxonomic groups

Running process:

filter_viral.py          -> data/processed/proteomes_filtered.tsv
                                       |
                                       v
mmseq_run.sh             -> data/raw/m8s/*.m8
                                       |
                                       v
filter_hits.py           -> data/processed/filtered_hits.json
                                       |
                                       v
extract_sequences.py     -> data/processed/class1_sequences.fasta
                            data/processed/class2_sequences.fasta
                                       |
                                       v
clean_sequences.py       -> data/processed/class1_sequences.fasta  (in-place)
                            data/processed/class2_sequences.fasta  (in-place)
                                       |
                                       v
generate_tables.py       -> results/stats/table1_class1.csv
                            results/stats/table2_class2.csv
